{
  "$comment": "Single source of truth for which prompt and model runs each task. Swapping a model or bumping a prompt is an edit here, not a code change. Every task's model_id and version get persisted with whatever the call produced (D5). Nested blocks are ADK workflow sub-agents, addressed with dotted keys: llm.run('question-builder.validator', ...).",
  "$models": "Verified against a live API key on 2026-08-22, not taken from documentation. gemini-3.7-flash is GA, fast (~2s) and was accurate in a structured-output probe. gemini-3.1-pro-preview is slower (~4.5s) and carries preview risk, so it is used only where reasoning depth genuinely pays: decisions about a person, and the anchors lane 2 scores against. If a preview model is withdrawn mid-hackathon, gemini-3.7-flash is the drop-in replacement everywhere. Note gemini-3.6-flash failed the probe by extracting a person's name as a skill.",
